  "subtitle": "A motorized rotating tower that keeps the game's secrets behind a tinted cover",
  "why_scout_cares": "The computer is a physical black tower that swivels to face each player, conceals its state behind a tinted plastic cover, and reveals events by rotating an internal carousel of backlit film cels plus a hidden LED readout. Play is an embodied ritual of rotating the tower, pressing membrane buttons, and watching the state physically spin into view. A TMS-1400 chip runs the whole secret. The interaction is the tower's conceal-and-reveal theater.",
